1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,700
Where are we going?

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,400
We're joining a mixer.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,740
They're so kind.

4
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:10,760
I didn't want them

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:16,470
to feel forced to like me.

6
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:20,790
What I want isn't something like that.

7
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:24,000
Why don't you open up to them like this?

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,830
Tell them you're feeling confused,

9
00:00:25,830 --> 00:00:29,070
and tangled up inside.

10
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,380
I'm sure they'll understand.

11
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:35,520
What misunderstanding?

12
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:39,000
I didn't want you to "like" me out of pity,

13
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,530
and not actually feel that way.

14
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,300
I...

15
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:48,820
I want to be with you whenever I can.

16
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:55,220
What do you mean when you "like" me?

17
00:00:56,870 --> 00:01:01,310
I want to touch you.

18
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:05,010
I also want to hold hands with you.

19
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:08,150
I want to hug you tight, too.

20
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:10,260
That's what my "like" means.

21
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:29,610
See you soon, Kou.

22
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,510
[Morning]

23
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,530
[Are you still asleep?]

24
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,480
[I had a dream about you last night]

25
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:03,720
[What time should we head out today?]

26
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,400
[You're awake]

27
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,690
[Morning]

28
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:20,200
I'm heading out.

29
00:02:39,170 --> 00:02:42,040
Hello, I'm your boyfriend.

30
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,810
I know.

31
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:45,480
And you are?

32
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,160
Your boyfriend.

33
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:51,750
- Ready?
- Yeah.

34
00:02:58,710 --> 00:03:01,010
What time does your shift end today?

35
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:04,500
I'll be doing work until the evening.

36
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,330
Sorry.

37
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:07,740
Huh?

38
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,200
We just started dating, and I'm so busy...

39
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,300
I'll be waiting for you to finish.

40
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:15,780
Okay.

41
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:20,030
- It's strange.
- Huh?

42
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:23,000
I thought my love for you maxed out,

43
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,910
but now that we're dating, I love you more.

44
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:30,700
Oh, uh...

45
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:34,180
I don't know how to respond.

46
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,150
Too heavy?

47
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,870
No, not at all...

48
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:39,890
Your bag.

49
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:41,510
I'll carry it for you.

50
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,280
Thanks.

51
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,930
I'm racking up "boyfriend points".

52
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:51,080
If I get to ten, I get a kiss.

53
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:17,650
See you later.

54
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,070
I'm walking you in, not trespassing.

55
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:28,150
Whatever you say.

56
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:47,860
I'm charging up till the evening.

57
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,230
What am I, an energy drink?

58
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:56,570
Mayama.

59
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:58,240
Now?

60
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,800
Now.

61
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,270
I'll come get you once you're done.

62
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:15,280
See you later.

63
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:31,130
Bye for now.

64
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,880
That's playing dirty.

65
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,810
Thanks.

66
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:36,380
Are you free next Saturday?

67
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,760
Why?

68
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:41,300
Check it out.

69
00:06:44,410 --> 00:06:47,680
A Tanabata Festival.
[T/N: July 7th; known as the Star Festival]

70
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,340
It's happening by your place, right?

71
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,860
Yeah.

72
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:54,510
I can't believe it's almost July.

73
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:58,850
Want to go together?

74
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:01,910
Hold on.

75
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:07,070
- Is that a no?
- No, but...

76
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:09,190
I knew it.

77
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:12,510
I'm scheduled to work at an event that day.

78
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:14,680
- I see.
- I'm free the day after.

79
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:16,080
Let's find another festival to go to.

80
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,610
Sorry, I'm only free that Saturday.

81
00:07:18,610 --> 00:07:21,880
I have summer school the rest of our break.

82
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:27,310
My Mayama battery will run out...

83
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:30,410
Sorry.

84
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,280
Nah, I share the blame there.

85
00:07:38,670 --> 00:07:43,230
It'd be nice if we could do something
that screams "summer".

86
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,640
For real?

87
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,450
- Loser pays the bill.
- Deal.

88
00:08:01,450 --> 00:08:04,310
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

89
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:14,820
Puppy!

90
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:17,290
Come take a break.

91
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:24,980
- Great work out there.
- Thank you.

92
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:26,200
It's so hot in here...

93
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,170
I'd bet.

94
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:31,650
- Here, stay hydrated.
- Thank you.

95
00:08:32,550 --> 00:08:38,020
<i>I didn't think the "event"
would be a Tanabata festival.</i>

96
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:42,780
When you're ready, could you pass out
these wishing slips to guests?

97
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:45,350
- Sure.
- Thank you so much!

98
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:47,550
You must be melting in there.

99
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:50,270
No one wanted to wear the suit,

100
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:52,760
but someone had to do it.

101
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,650
I'm glad you volunteered.

102
00:08:54,650 --> 00:08:57,840
I put the slips right there for you.

103
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:02,520
<i>This was the festival where it happened.</i>

104
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:05,000
What are you talking about?

105
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:10,250
Dude, obviously we were joking.

106
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:13,730
She'd never confess to a guy like you.

107
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:24,190
<i>I remembered something I'd rather forget.</i>

108
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,780
Thanks.

109
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:42,150
Asamiya?

110
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:49,130
Thank you!

111
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,610
<i>Why is he here?</i>

112
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:57,460
<i>I told him I couldn't go today.</i>

113
00:09:57,460 --> 00:10:00,590
Kou!

114
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:04,920
Sheesh, don't leave me behind.

115
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,460
<i>Huh?</i>

116
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:09,170
Say what?

117
00:10:09,170 --> 00:10:11,250
He spoke.

118
00:10:15,570 --> 00:10:18,740
Where to go...

119
00:10:20,650 --> 00:10:23,070
Hey, let's grab a wishing slip.

120
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:24,040
I'm good.

121
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,450
What? Buzzkill.

122
00:10:27,450 --> 00:10:30,440
Could I get a wishing slip?

123
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:39,470
Hello?

124
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:45,850
Thank you.

125
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:48,930
I feel like he's staring daggers into me.

126
00:10:48,930 --> 00:10:50,400
You're imagining things.

127
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:53,430
If you say so.
Come on, let's go see the stalls.

128
00:10:53,430 --> 00:10:56,340
I'm craving shaved ice.

129
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:58,670
Do you want some?

130
00:11:04,290 --> 00:11:07,170
Festivals are great.

131
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:09,870
I really feel like I'm back in Japan now.

132
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:13,740
Thanks for coming with me.

133
00:11:15,730 --> 00:11:20,670
<i>What's her relationship with Asamiya?</i>

134
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:25,680
I was so worried about you
while I was abroad.

135
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,450
Really now.

136
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:40,410
- They're here?
- Yeah.

137
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:42,140
They're looking this way.

138
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:17,590
<i>Was he using me forget the loneliness
of his girlfriend being overseas?</i>

139
00:12:24,050 --> 00:12:27,120
<i>Was I just the substitute until she returned?</i>

140
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:31,910
I know what you consider your faults.

141
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:38,750
But all that has made me
fall for you even more.

142
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,210
I obviously meant it romantically.

143
00:12:50,810 --> 00:12:54,290
<i>No. Asamiya would never do that.</i>

144
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:56,780
<i>I should ask him about her first.</i>

145
00:12:57,450 --> 00:13:00,350
Huh? Mayama?

146
00:13:00,350 --> 00:13:01,490
Kagami...

147
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,020
I haven't seen you in ages.

148
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:05,230
What's with the getup?

149
00:13:05,230 --> 00:13:06,800
Holy cow.

150
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:10,110
Are they still there?

151
00:13:12,830 --> 00:13:15,690
Nope. They're gone.

152
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,450
Hey, did I just hear a sigh?

153
00:13:19,450 --> 00:13:22,910
You wish you had a cute girlfriend like me.

154
00:13:22,910 --> 00:13:24,720
That's some self-confidence.

155
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:27,910
You know, I feel bad
for whoever was in that suit.

156
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:30,320
They must be melting.

157
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:34,300
I know someone who'd immediately
volunteer for something like that.

158
00:13:42,050 --> 00:13:43,370
Wait, him?

159
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:46,070
Yeah. He's the one
who fell for that confession.

160
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:49,510
I laughed so hard, my stomach hurt!

161
00:13:51,010 --> 00:13:54,360
I'd never work here if I were you.

162
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,290
Yeah, seriously.

163
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,800
Hey, you're not in a festive mood.

164
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,020
- I am.
- You should let him have a date.

165
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,250
- Yeah!
- What? Why?

166
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:05,080
We wanna lift Mayama's spirits.

167
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,310
What?

168
00:14:06,310 --> 00:14:09,580
I'm already dating someone right now.

169
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:10,800
- What?
- No way.

170
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:14,220
- You're lying.
- Yeah.

171
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:17,510
Come on, don't be shy.

172
00:14:17,510 --> 00:14:20,500
Just take a lap around the festival.

173
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,720
Sounds good to me.

174
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,520
Yeah, go for it!

175
00:14:24,790 --> 00:14:26,650
Kagami.

176
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:28,230
What?

177
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,950
Don't be such a killjoy, go.

178
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:35,280
- Yeah.
- She's waiting.

179
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,360
No.

180
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,960
Huh?

181
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:41,280
I don't want to.

182
00:14:42,810 --> 00:14:45,800
You say you were just joking.

183
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:49,150
But that really hurt my feelings.

184
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,150
I don't want to see you guys anymore.

185
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:54,600
- Huh?
- What gives?

186
00:14:55,920 --> 00:15:00,200
We're your only friends, so suck it up.

187
00:15:02,910 --> 00:15:08,420
I have other friends now.
Ones who actually care.

188
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,180
Go with her. Now.

189
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:24,850
Don't touch him.

190
00:15:24,850 --> 00:15:26,890
Who the hell are you?

191
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:31,660
I'm Mayama's friend. Unlike you jerks.

192
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:33,180
Huh?

193
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:37,130
Hey, ouch!

194
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:42,700
Don't mess with Mayama ever again.

195
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:49,990
Let's ditch these losers.

196
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:51,500
Yeah.

197
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,240
Mayama...

198
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:08,520
I'm glad you're okay.

199
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,080
Thank you.

200
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,440
Sorry.

201
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,780
I should have noticed sooner.

202
00:16:27,350 --> 00:16:30,590
Did I gain extra "boyfriend points"?

203
00:16:34,270 --> 00:16:35,870
Mayama?

204
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:41,860
Who was that?

205
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:44,840
Huh?

206
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,800
I saw you two going around together.

207
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:56,180
You and that pretty lady, arm-in-arm.

208
00:16:56,770 --> 00:16:57,940
That's my...

209
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,510
Kou!

210
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:01,550
Jeez, there you are.

211
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:05,700
I was looking everywhere for you.

212
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:10,600
Huh? Who's this?

213
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,780
My friend, Mayama.

214
00:17:16,750 --> 00:17:19,390
Thanks for tolerating my little brother.

215
00:17:19,390 --> 00:17:21,950
I'm Kou's sister, Koiro Asamiya.

216
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,000
Huh?

217
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,810
Your sister?

218
00:17:31,810 --> 00:17:33,220
We look nothing alike, right?

219
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:36,700
But you were walking with your arms linked...

220
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:39,990
Some girl has been coming onto me, hard.

221
00:17:39,990 --> 00:17:42,090
She was following me around all day.

222
00:17:42,090 --> 00:17:46,020
Yeah. So, I pretended to be his girlfriend.

223
00:17:46,650 --> 00:17:50,230
I didn't think you'd see us.

224
00:17:50,950 --> 00:17:54,180
So, that's what was going on.

225
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:59,620
Mayama, right?

226
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,170
Yes.

227
00:18:04,490 --> 00:18:06,710
Take care of my brother for me.

228
00:18:08,010 --> 00:18:10,640
I know he's a bit overbearing.

229
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,590
Not at all.

230
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,850
- Don't badmouth me.
- Sorry.

231
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:15,650
Oh, I know.

232
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:20,120
Here.

233
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:21,610
And here.

234
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:23,550
Go make a wish.

235
00:18:26,490 --> 00:18:28,570
Go on.

236
00:18:28,570 --> 00:18:31,070
Make a wish!

237
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,620
What did you write?

238
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,270
I'm not telling.

239
00:18:39,270 --> 00:18:40,940
Aw, come on.

240
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,080
Where should I hang yours?

241
00:18:55,150 --> 00:18:57,260
What did you write?

242
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:58,550
It's a secret.

243
00:18:58,550 --> 00:19:01,560
If I tell you, it won't come true.

244
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:04,450
Then mine's a secret, too.

245
00:19:06,950 --> 00:19:10,600
<i>Our annual finale of the Tanabata Festival,</i>

246
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:13,400
<i>the fireworks show, is about to begin.</i>

247
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:17,860
<i>We hope it will serve as
a wonderful summer memory.</i>

248
00:19:18,570 --> 00:19:20,720
They're doing fireworks.

249
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:23,370
- Come with me.
- Huh?

250
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,860
I know the best viewing spot.

251
00:19:30,990 --> 00:19:33,050
Hey, wait.

252
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:34,500
Slow down.

253
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,420
Are we walking any farther?

254
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:39,430
No.

255
00:19:39,430 --> 00:19:41,220
We're here.

256
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,950
Look.

257
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:49,380
Wow...

258
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:56,970
I happened to find this spot
while running away in shame

259
00:19:56,970 --> 00:20:00,170
from that whole confession prank.

260
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:09,370
These fireworks saved me in a way.

261
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:21,950
Doesn't it hurt to remember?

262
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:31,560
Not anymore. I have you now.

263
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:45,500
Let's watch the fireworks.

264
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:49,410
I'm glad.

265
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:53,240
We managed to do one "summer" thing.

266
00:21:52,010 --> 00:21:56,700
[I wish for Mayama to find happiness]

267
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:02,520
[I wish to find happiness with Asamiya]

268
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:28,050
My sister's staying with a friend tonight.

269
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:35,920
My parents are on vacation,
and aren't home either.

270
00:22:42,510 --> 00:22:44,740
Want to come over?

271
00:22:46,510 --> 00:22:47,970
Huh?

272
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:50,480
Is that a no?

273
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:58,010
No, it's not exactly a no.

274
00:23:00,820 --> 00:23:04,670
I'm not ready to let you go home yet.

275
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:32,500
I don't need to slam the breaks anymore.

276
00:24:32,500 --> 00:24:35,830
Should we tell Sakaki
and Tsunekawada about us?

277
00:24:35,830 --> 00:24:37,890
- I wouldn't want to...
- No.

278
00:24:37,890 --> 00:24:39,280
We never know who's watching.

279
